							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1399.msg14224#msg14224">Quote from: Shakro on February 03, 2005, 06:18:17 pm</a></div><div class="quote">If the process of leveling is tedious, then why do it?&nbsp; Surely you can find a game to play that&#039;s not tedious, counterstrike or halo or GTA3 or something?&nbsp; <br /></div><br />That&#039;s why the whole &quot;quest&quot; based system was used in WoW, together with lesser amounts of experience required to level - to make levelling feel less like a chore and more fun.&nbsp; It allows one to avoid the whole &quot;grinding&quot; concept in EQ, i.e. sitting on your ass in one spot for hours on end, pulling single mobs, kill, pull next mob, kill, etc.<br /><br />Obviously, even questing gets repetitive after a while, and tediousness sets in.&nbsp; No MMORPG will ever be able to avoid a certain degree of repetitiveness (which leads to tediousness).&nbsp; My guess is Blizzard&#039;s hope is that by the time that occurs, you will be at or near the end game.&nbsp; For me, the system works - levelling in WoW doesn&#039;t seem like a chore so far.&nbsp; Getting through level 59 in EQ when Kunark was released was just a pain in the ass.&nbsp; There was nothing fun about it - I&#039;d been killing frogs in Sebilis for nearly 8 levels by that time.&nbsp; And when I finally reached 60, I didn&#039;t have this magical sense of accomplishment - my feelings would best be characterized as &quot;Thank God that is over.&nbsp; I hope I never have to do that again.&quot;<br /><br />Bottom line:&nbsp; Finding the correct levelling curve in MMORPGs can be tricky.&nbsp; You obviously want players to take time exploring the content and enjoying themselves, but you don&#039;t want it to feel like a chore.&nbsp; If the levelling curve is really large, it will inevitably start to feel like a chore instead of being fun.&nbsp; For some people, this happens within a month of playing any MMORPG.&nbsp; I find the levelling curve in WoW just fine and the game&#039;s &quot;fun&quot; factor would not be enhanced by doubling or tripling the amount of experience required to level.
