							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Yep, the Dungeons and instances can be a blast. I generally was able to average a level a night when I wanted to up to about level 50 or so. After that, the quests can be more challenging, and require more grouping to accomplish, unless you&#039;re just plain bullheaded like myself and find ways to get them done solo.<br /><br />Hunters have that in the bag too. Best memory to date, a quest in Andorhol Ruins, have to get a book from inside the town hall that is surrounded by undead, with an elite or two thown in for good measure. <br /><br />After checking tracking, and looking around the building, I guessed there were no mobs inside, and made a made dash for the doorway, and ran inside with a sizable train on my tail.<br /><br />So I get inside, and feign death... (OMG yes, hunters get FD at level 40!) bye bye train.<br /><br />See books laying all over the place, and proceed to pick one up, and two more elites spawn on my happy tail. Summon my pet, and held them off for a short period till FD refreshes, and survived. So now I&#039;m laying there, wondering what the fook to do now, and they despawn after a couple minutes.<br /><br />So I repeat, and am able to FD before they stun me or anything after I loot the book again. Finally found the one I wanted, and did the train and FD thing to get back out.<br /><br />Under normal rules, I would have needed a full group with a good tank, and healing to bash my way through. Using a little luck, and brains, I managed to solo a tough quest.<br /><br />These are the things I love to do, and mean more than anything else to me personally.
