							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Something a few of you have said reminds me of this noob experience I had back in July-ish 2001 when I first started EQ...please bare with me while I share it with you.. <br /><br />One of my most memorable experiences on EQ was when I was level 5 and had played a few days. I was bound in West Freeport and my best friend, Seeate (druid) had sent me the game CD to get me to play with him, and gave me my first noob gear and like 20pp, which was a lot because mobs dropped 5 coppers. I was grateful to him for his generosity and guidance. <br /><br />Anyway, he ported us so we could get to GFay for a quick trade skill lesson before he logged for the night. On the tip-toppest platform in the tree houses, he told me not to get myself dead or anything after he logged.... which made me laugh and I promised I&#039;d only combine a couple more arrows and then camp out too.<br /><br />No sooner had he poofed did I fall outta that tree-house to my death. I swear, under 20 seconds later. Well great!&nbsp; I have no idea how, why, wtf I did that for. Now I&#039;m bound in W Freeport and my body is in Gfay and I don&#039;t have any clue how to get it and I have under 30 minutes before it rots. Boats unknown to me and as the lostest player in game I&#039;d never of made it in time. Not even close!<br /><br />Standing at the gate in WFP I see another player sit, as if to camp, so I quickly sent him a tell. &#039;I&#039;ve died and my corpse will rot unless I get to it in time... Is there any possible way he could help me.?&quot;&nbsp; I told him what happened and that I had about 15-20 minutes to get my corpse and he not only agreed to help me but was a druid too! What luck!&nbsp; He asks &quot;Where did you die?&quot; I replied proud because I remembered the name of the land where my corpse was . . . &quot;Norrath!&quot; <br /><br />This guy ports us to Butchers Block. He provides me safe passage and the /follow ability, runs me thru Gfay, and asks me where my corpse is which I know for a fact is on the ground under a tree house (somewhere), with my impeccable details on the directions.. He gets me to my corpse.. Yay!.. My hero and with minutes to spare!&nbsp; I was so grateful to this player I tried to give him any of the (crap) loot on me and/or the 20pp Seeate had given me. I was soo grateful but he accepts nothing and he was happy to help. <br /><br />The reason I&#039;ve never forgot this story is simple.&nbsp; EverQuest FORCED us to talk to each other.&nbsp; It FORCED us to interact with each other.&nbsp; It forced players to be dependant on other players. It made us be socialable... and more social then the forums we religiously drop in on...<br /><br />Before PoP and even probably Luclin&#039;s spires.... druids and wizzies had to port us almost everywhere.&nbsp; And before potions and right clickies... we had to rely on other classes for almost EVERYTHING we did! Period. Unless you LOVE to solo and are good at it, you had to be on the same side of the team. That&#039;s one of the things that made the game so incredible. <br /><br />I switched mains to a cleric a long time ago. Nowadays, I know about twenty (AT LEAST) people who can, will, and do box a cleric (healer...whatever class...etc)&nbsp; in their regular groups. It&#039;s a hardship when groups are so self sufficient being played by one or two people, that you&#039;re left with nothing to do but watch grass grow because nobody needs you to join them.<br /><br />Okay. The end.&nbsp; I&#039;ll stop my rambling and thank you all for listening to my 2 cents. If it was worth even that. <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" />&nbsp; *hugs ya&#039;ll*&nbsp; Even the brats who snuck off to another game.
